#== News

== About me
I am a postdoctoral researcher with a joint appointment in the [https://statistics.berkeley.edu/ Department of Statistics] at University of California, Berkeley, and [https://www.icsi.berkeley.edu/ International Computer Science Institute], working with [https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~mmahoney/index.html Michael Mahoney]. I received my Ph.D. from the Department of Mathematics at University of California San Diego, where I was fortunate to be advised by [https://math.ucsd.edu/people/profiles/ioana-dumitriu Ioana Dumitriu] and [https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~tkemp/ Todd Kemp]. 

#== Education 

== Research Interests
My current research focuses on developing the mathematical foundations of artificial intelligence, especially in deep learning, using tools from high-dimensional probability.
- Deep Learning Theory and Foundations of AI
- Randomized Numerical Linear Algebra and Optimization in LLM
- Random Matrix Theory and Free Probability Theory



